WEBVTT

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:03.498
Prac360 connects every practice that uses it.

00:00:03.498 --> 00:00:15.787
In this short video we'll show how a patient gives consent to share their clinical records, how they use the Prac360 patient app, and how doctors across the Prac360 network work from one shared file.

00:00:16.488 --> 00:00:20.034
Every patient is linked by one Prac360 patient ID:

00:00:20.034 --> 00:00:23.012
their South African ID or passport number.

00:00:23.012 --> 00:00:27.692
Until the patient agrees, each practice only sees its own records.

00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:29.890
David's file is not shared yet.

00:00:30.591 --> 00:00:35.069
At the practice, reception reads this short explanation to the patient.

00:00:35.069 --> 00:00:37.024
It covers all clinical records:

00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:43.079
consultation notes, medicines and allergies, results, letters, hospital admissions and oncology.

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:46.422
Accounts, payments and appointments are never shared.

00:00:47.122 --> 00:00:48.582
The consent is recorded:

00:00:48.582 --> 00:00:52.841
who gave it, how it was given, and which staff member was the witness.

00:00:52.841 --> 00:00:56.674
A short video, like this one, is right here to help explain it.

00:00:57.823 --> 00:01:01.740
Patients can also do this themselves, in the Prac360 patient app.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.091
Here is a preview of how the app works.

00:01:06.023 --> 00:01:10.071
In the app, David sees every clinical record Prac360 holds on his ID:

00:01:10.071 --> 00:01:19.164
his medicines and conditions, his hospital admission after a heart attack, and his oncology treatment plan, each marked with the practice that recorded it.

00:01:21.586 --> 00:01:27.590
Under Sharing, he reads exactly what is shared, ticks that he understands, and taps Give consent.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:29.386
Sharing is on, straight away.

00:01:33.786 --> 00:01:40.183
Back at the practice, David's file now shows that he gave consent in the app, and the combined file is one click away.

00:01:42.987 --> 00:01:47.701
Any Prac360 doctor who treats David now opens one combined, read only file:

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:54.931
allergies, medicines, conditions, oncology and hospital admissions, each marked with the practice that recorded it.

00:01:54.931 --> 00:01:57.948
And every time someone opens it, it is recorded.

00:02:00.192 --> 00:02:06.452
David can book any doctor in the Prac360 network, at this practice or at another network practice.

00:02:06.452 --> 00:02:09.455
He picks a doctor and a time for his follow-up.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:11.904
He confirms.

00:02:11.904 --> 00:02:17.732
The app reminds him that, because sharing is on, the doctor can already see his full clinical file.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.245
The booking lands straight in the practice diary, marked as booked in the patient app.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:28.513
When David arrives, his doctor has his full history ready.

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:31.911
David stays in control.

00:02:31.911 --> 00:02:39.887
In the app he can see who looked at his file, and he can stop sharing at any time, in the app or at any practice, and sharing stops at once.

00:02:41.813 --> 00:02:42.329
Prac360:

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:47.746
one patient, one shared file, across the whole network, with the patient in control.

00:02:47.746 --> 00:02:52.003
The patient app shown here is a preview of the app that is coming.

